class:: SpectralFrameOsc
summary:: Phase-continuous synthesis from interpolated spectral frames
categories:: UGens>Generators>Additive
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

SpectralFrameOsc maintains an independent signed phase for every stored partial
while interpolating ratios and amplitudes between spectral frames. Ratio
stretch, dB-per-octave tilt, neighbor blur, Nyquist fades, and smoothly changing
partial activation are applied before energy normalization. This is an
original generic resynthesis engine; it does not analyze sound files.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Klang::. Both sum sinusoidal
components, but SpectralFrameOsc preserves per-partial phase while continuously
moving through Buffer-stored spectra.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: bufnum
Mono Buffer prepared by link::Classes/SpectralFrameBuffer::.

argument:: freq
Signed reference frequency in hertz.

argument:: frame
Continuous frame index, wrapped across the stored frame count.

argument:: stretch
Exponent applied to ratios as code::ratio.pow(stretch)::, clamped to
code::-4..4::.

argument:: tilt
Amplitude slope in decibels per octave of ratio, clamped to code::-48..48::.

argument:: blur
Neighbor-amplitude smoothing amount, clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: activePartials
Continuous active-partial count. Entries and exits use a short gain ramp.

argument:: phaseMode
Initialization-rate phase layout: code::0:: aligned, code::1:: evenly spread,
or code::2:: seeded random.

argument:: frames
Initialization-rate number of frames in the Buffer, from code::1:: through
code::65536::.

argument:: partials
Initialization-rate partial count from code::1:: through code::1024::.

argument:: seed
Initialization-rate nonnegative seed for phase mode code::2::.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
One normalized audio signal.

method:: kr

SpectralFrameOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Phase identity is attached to partial index. If ratios cross while frames
interpolate, phases do not exchange identities. A malformed, freed, or
reallocated Buffer permanently silences the active instance without logging
from the real-time callback.

The calculation path is selected when the Synth is constructed. Audio-rate
code::frame::, code::stretch::, code::tilt::, code::blur::, or
code::activePartials:: selects an exact per-sample evaluator. Scalar and
control-rate versions of all five controls select a lower-cost block-cooked
path with ramped weights and recursive complex oscillators. The optimized path
still advances inactive phase identities analytically, so bringing a partial
back does not reset its phase. The instance owns about code::64 * partials::
bytes of private state in addition to the shared Buffer.

examples::

code::
(
Routine({
    var bank;
    SpectralFrameBuffer.prepare(
        s,
        [
            [[1, 2, 3, 4], [1, 0.5, 0.25, 0.1]],
            [[1, 1.6, 2.8, 5], [1, 0.2, 0.7, 0.12]]
        ],
        action: { |object| bank = object }
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        SpectralFrameOsc.ar(
            bank.buffer, 75,
            frame: LFTri.kr(0.08).range(0, 1),
            frames: bank.frames, partials: bank.partials
        ) * 0.07
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

code::
(
Routine({
    var bank;
    SpectralFrameBuffer.prepare(
        s,
        [
            [[1, 2, 4, 7], [1, 0.5, 0.2, 0.08]],
            [[1, 3, 5, 9], [1, 0.7, 0.3, 0.1]]
        ],
        action: { |object| bank = object }
    );
    s.sync;
    {
        SpectralFrameOsc.ar(
            bank.buffer, 52, frame: SinOsc.kr(0.07).range(0, 1),
            stretch: MouseX.kr(0.5, 1.6), tilt: -2,
            blur: 0.3, activePartials: 4,
            frames: bank.frames, partials: bank.partials
        ) * 0.06
    }.play;
}).play;
)
::

